                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h3]Remember the dinosaur from Chrome when you don't have Internet?\nThis is him now.[/h3]\n\nFrom gameplay perspective this is mainly about ponies jumping and trying to avoid the fences. But as you know, this is a little bit cursed this time. I have played Inscryption before this game, so I knew what to expect from this developer and was not dissapointed. \n\nAt times, this game feels like proto-inscryption, with some ideas and twists already there, but with execution pretty minimalistic and simple. But anyway, that was a fun time. I didn't notice how the time passed, the same premise keeps being fun with a lot of new variations that make it not just interesting, but even...funny? \n\nThis game tries to be scary with all these fourth-wall-breaking sequences and changing shapes faster than you get bored, but these things made me smiling on how creative such a simple game can be! This is definitely a good start to Daniel Mullins Games if you have never played his games before.\n\nNow I'm waiting for Pony Island 2 and can't imagine how insane it will be!",
